# Where this machine keeps the game. Copy to `.env` and edit; `.env` is not committed.
#
# This file DECIDES. The editor reads its folders from here, from the environment,
# or from `--game=`/`--data=` on the command line, and from nowhere else — there
# is no settings file behind it and nothing guesses a folder. Say nothing and the
# setup window opens and asks, then writes this file for you.
#
# Precedence, most specific first: the command line, then the shell's own
# variables, then this file.
#
# One per checkout, so a worktree can work against its own copy of the game
# without touching anybody else's.
#
# Read by the editor only. The e2e suite keeps its own explicit variables: to it
# HOMM5_ROOT means "the install to play in", and its default is a throwaway under
# _tmp so a run cannot leave `e2e …` maps in a real game folder.

# The Heroes 5 install: holds data/*.pak and bin/, and gets our H5E/ folder.
HOMM5_ROOT=C:\Games\Steam\steamapps\common\Heroes of Might and Magic 5 Tribes of the East

# Where those archives are unpacked to — the tree the editor reads.
HOMM5_DATA=C:\Games\Steam\steamapps\common\Heroes of Might and Magic 5 Tribes of the East\homm5-editor\data-unpacked
